Persistent cloud density and illumination volume
================================================

Authority and scope
  Source: docs/PBR.CloudVolume.Proposal.md, complete proposal including Traversal acceleration candidates.
  Context: docs/PBR.Clouds.md and docs/PBR.Atmosphere.Publication.md; existing consumer/GPU contracts.
  User invocation authorizes this new plan, not runtime implementation. Execute only requested phases.
  Proposal decisions remain unresolved: Phase 1 resolves them before implementation proceeds. The
    illustrative memory table and old lighting-only constants are not selected defaults.
  This plan owns a new removable candidate. PBR.CloudLightingVolume.todo and PBR.CloudRealtime.todo
    retain separate authority; no old completion receipts count as implementation of this design.
  Stored 3D density is authoritative for view, direct and diffuse integration. Native descriptors
    feed generation only; procedural density must not reappear as a per-ray fallback.
  Preserve finite native coverage, placement/wind identity, physical units, both PBR modes, depth,
    atmosphere and six-attachment OIT contracts. Sampled density is an explicit shape approximation.
  Start with shallow anisotropic dense storage, shared density/lighting lattice and coarse occupancy,
    subject to the Phase 1 feasibility gate. Sparse bricks/clipmaps require a proposal revision if
    needed; separate lighting resolution is a later measured optimization, not implicit scope.
  No replacement weather, general path tracer, widely spaced slice rendering, required screen-space
    temporal accumulation, migration, generic rendering framework or automatic old-candidate removal.
  Initial correctness view is full-resolution OIT. Reduced-resolution spatial reconstruction is a
    separate later decision. No claim that persistent lighting eliminates final view integration.

Execution and evidence (applies to every phase)
  Use PBR/Clouds/Volume/ and private shaders/cloud_volume/ under the production project. Keep files
    responsibility-focused and roots thin; document classes/methods and follow visibility regions.
  Candidate depends on public/native scene contracts and general infrastructure, not existing cloud
    transport/shadow/reconstruction algorithms or lighting-only resource owners. Use existing GPU,
    program, binding, submission and barrier abstractions in production and tests; no raw GL fixtures.
  Run builds/tests through subagents. Use cached incremental builds and affected contract checks only;
    reuse unchanged passing evidence. Expand checks only for concrete changes, failures or evidence gaps.
  No routine clean/full-catalog rebuild, full baseline matrix or packaging during implementation.
    Investigate unexpected broad rebuilds; reserve frozen-candidate packaging/matrix work for Phase 9.
  No approximation-quality, convergence, image-difference, noise or visual-fidelity test thresholds.
    Tests cover declared math, finite values, units, resource identity/lifetime, publication and bounds.
    Reuse focused fixtures and avoid redundant cases. Never raise budgets to satisfy approximation tests.
  Distinguish source review, focused/headless evidence, measured GPU cost, package and user appearance.
    Never launch/close the game; honor the user's running-game choice and disclose timing contention.
  Before completion, reconcile proposal coverage, review changes and record proportionate evidence.
    Permanent architecture docs describe delivered behavior only; later phases remain unchecked.

Phase 1 - Select the representation and numerical contract
  Outcome: concrete reviewed constants and publication rules make implementation feasible without
    silently substituting the old lighting-only design.
  [ ] Resolve resident memory ceiling and smallest cloud feature worth preserving with the user.
      Select finite horizontal coverage, vertical coverage/margin, anisotropic dimensions, guards
      and region/block sizes together. Document representable feature scale and filtering softness.
  [ ] Calculate complete resident and peak replacement memory: 22 bytes/voxel base fields plus guards,
      metadata, occupancy, scratch and any justified transient allocation. Include copy bandwidth.
      If dense coverage is unaffordable, stop downstream implementation and revise the proposal for
      an explicitly selected alternative; do not silently clip coverage or restore procedural lookup.
  [ ] Specify stable material keys, camera independence, wind transform once, circular addressing,
      filtered seam adjacency, finite empty guards and bounded coordinate arithmetic.
  [ ] Specify density cell-average coverage, connected-face/detail generation, units, half-float
      representability, generation quadrature and neighbor influence. Select initialization and
      out-of-band replacement policy, including retained age and failure behavior.
  [ ] Specify direct integration, relevant-source rules and any explicit distance truncation.
      Specify diffuse recurrence/direction weights/albedo/environment boundary, first-scattering
      separation, finite radiance bounds, exposure-independent encoding and field/scale publication.
      Do not copy old counts/distances/budgets without an independent recorded rationale.
  [ ] Specify metadata granularity and alpha use only if required; initialized lighting fallback,
      stale/invalid distinctions, source/geometry change dependencies and transition policy.
  [ ] Select density/direct/diffuse work limits, fairness, source revisions, bounded initialization,
      and failure atomicity. Specify copy-before-partial-diffuse-update and its charged cost.
  [ ] Evaluate coarse DDA versus signed/unsigned distance bounds and hybrid maintenance requirements.
      Select an initial strategy (coarse DDA is the proposal's first candidate); identify whether a
      distance prototype is justified for Phase 8. Do not mandate two production structures.
  [ ] Derive view/transport traversal limits from admitted extent and spacing, including empty-block
      traversal. Retain the half-voxel axis rule for the initial view; no silent cap-induced coarsening.
  [ ] Record selected settings/compiled options and source decisions in the proposal; flag any changed
      architectural assumption for agreement before dependent work. Review arithmetic and coverage.
  [ ] Completion: no implementation-critical constants or publication semantics remain implicit;
      memory/feature tradeoff is agreed and the selected specification reconciles with the proposal.

Phase 2 - Own stable volume storage and publication
  Depends on: Phase 1.
  Outcome: an isolated, bounded volume can be initialized, retained and retired safely.
  [ ] Implement domain/addressing and owned R16F density, RG16F visibility and two RGBA16F diffuse
      fields, region metadata and selected occupancy storage through existing abstractions.
      Admit actual device format/dimension limits and checked memory totals before allocation.
  [ ] Initialize all texels to defined density/lighting values. Implement hardware trilinear samplers
      plus exact region identity, without manual eight-fetch interpolation or validity hiding density.
  [ ] Preserve overlapping material cells on recenter, initialize entering slabs/guards and distinguish
      circular seams from finite edges. Revoke unrelated identities on replacement/reset.
  [ ] Implement bounded startup/replacement and height expansion policy; retain the last coherent
      publication during pending changes and release partial allocations on failure.
  [ ] Implement field/scale/revision publication and ordered read/write boundaries. Justify any spare
      beyond diffuse ping-pong by an actual hazard; no default descriptor/flag/remap allocation stack.
  [ ] Verify focused addressing, seam/guard, format/accounting, identity and cleanup contracts; update
      current architecture documentation for storage delivered here. Use incremental validation only.
  [ ] Completion: stored fields have coherent identity and usable initialization within the agreed
      resident/peak budget, including recenter/replacement/failure paths.

Phase 3 - Generate persistent volumetric density
  Depends on: Phase 2.
  Outcome: native weather produces stored 3D shape that all later ray consumers can share.
  [ ] Capture certified native descriptors synchronously; retain no borrowed native texture across
      callbacks. Observe content changes without treating publication generation alone as a reset.
  [ ] Implement generation-only native cuboid overlap/coverage, connected faces and perturbation.
      Store cell-average extinction; thin cell intersections contribute under the selected contract.
  [ ] Implement bounded density jobs and content revisions; coalesce observations without resetting
      pending age. Update neighbor influence; pure wind translation retains unchanged material data.
  [ ] Publish complete regions/boundaries after barriers, preserve unaffected data and expose spatial
      age differences. Handle out-of-band changes using the selected replacement policy.
  [ ] Update conservative occupancy with each density publication, including the hardware-filtering
      footprint. Revoke unsafe old empty certificates before new occupied density becomes readable.
  [ ] Verify declared coverage math, finite stored units, publication ordering and change retention
      with focused fixtures; no procedural approximation/image gate. Update density documentation.
  [ ] Completion: density and safe occupancy are persistent and inspectable; no ray shader needs
      native geometry or procedural detail to determine visible/transport density.

Phase 4 - Traverse stored density and schedule retained work
  Depends on: Phase 3.
  Outcome: bounded ray traversal and fair lighting jobs are ready for both transport solvers.
  [ ] Implement the selected initial traversal (coarse DDA unless Phase 1 explicitly revised it),
      retaining state across block boundaries. Support zero direction components, anisotropic cells,
      negative rays, finite edges and circular addressing with forward progress.
  [ ] Skip only certified empty support; preserve actual integration lengths and the selected occupied
      sampling rule. Avoid root restarts and silent work-limit truncation of admitted rays.
  [ ] Implement separate bounded direct/diffuse queues after density publication. Prioritize new/
      changed content and active/visible stale work, with fair offscreen service and persistent ages.
  [ ] Propagate nonlocal density demand conservatively, initially domain-wide if selected. Coalesce
      once per update; retain dirty state and actual completed revisions until successful work.
  [ ] Handle light direction, intensity/environment, activation and refinement demand independently.
      Fog/exposure/camera motion must not clear compatible volume history.
  [ ] Verify traversal coverage/progress, filter-support safety, fairness/work limits and failed-work
      stamps with focused contract checks. Document behavior; no full performance matrix here.
  [ ] Completion: traversal is bounded and conservative, and queued work cannot become falsely fresh
      through selection alone or indefinitely starve due to repeated content changes.

Phase 5 - Retain direct illumination through stored density
  Depends on: Phase 4.
  Outcome: published direct transmission is reused across views and frames.
  [ ] Implement selected direct integrals using density textures and traversal exclusively. Store solar/
      lunar transmission; honor the finite domain and label any selected transport-distance truncation.
  [ ] Dispatch only relevant-source work; prioritize activation, retain compatible direction-stale
      results and apply current source intensity later without recomputing unchanged transmission.
  [ ] Publish successful region results/revisions after barriers; missing illumination uses the selected
      finite fallback without hiding occupied clouds. Failure cannot certify partial output as current.
  [ ] Verify physical integration arithmetic, finite values, source activation/intensity behavior,
      disabled compiled paths and publication through focused existing abstractions. Update docs.
  [ ] Completion: direct lighting consumes published density only and remains reusable under compatible
      source changes with honest age/dependency metadata. Incremental validation receipts are recorded.

Phase 6 - Progressively transport diffuse illumination
  Depends on: Phase 5.
  Outcome: retained higher-order/environment source is refined under a fixed budget.
  [ ] Implement the specified recurrence using stored density/direct visibility and previous diffuse
      source; physical segment extinction/albedo and normalized direction weights govern transport.
  [ ] Include incoming environment once, traverse empty gaps, and keep outgoing first scattering
      separate from diffuse higher orders. Use selected finite radiance bounds/encoding.
  [ ] Copy published diffuse data to the destination before partial writes; preserve untouched values,
      perform selected updates from the coherent source, then publish field and scale together.
      Skip copy/swap for empty batches. Charge full copy traffic separately from solver work.
  [ ] Propagate refinement demand and retain stale illumination across ordinary atmosphere changes.
      Apply the agreed fallback/transition policy without mixing incompatible density identities.
  [ ] Verify declared recurrence/units, bounds, copy preservation, scale publication and failure rules
      with focused tests only; no convergence or reference-image threshold. Update current docs.
  [ ] Completion: bounded successful batches refine a coherent persistent source without double
      counting environment/first scattering or losing untouched regions.

Phase 7 - Draw and select the independent stored-volume candidate
  Depends on: Phase 6.
  Outcome: the user can select and inspect actual stored volumetric clouds in game.
  [ ] Implement full-resolution view integration from published density, visibility and diffuse
      textures only. Clip domain/material/particle/liquid intervals; use voxel-relative steps and
      actual clipped lengths with conservative empty skipping. No procedural fallback or old cap.
  [ ] Evaluate current directional phase response plus diffuse once; apply atmosphere/local-medium
      and scene encoding once. Preserve both PBR modes and six native OIT products.
  [ ] Admit retained-energy bounds and independent camera/atmosphere calibration identities through
      established scene contracts. Do not reserve radiance from current sources alone.
  [ ] Wire shader discovery/typed variants and one thin consumer into existing lifecycle/selection.
      Retire old consumers before activation; preserve Existing and lighting-only selections, native
      Off/Simple meanings, and recovery policy. No migration or hidden background candidate work.
  [ ] Expose selected settings through existing configuration, with disabled paths compiled out.
      Add focused diagnostics to the existing debug menu: density, region identity/age, fallback,
      pending/actual work and resident memory. Avoid ordinary-play synchronous readback.
  [ ] Document exact in-game selection/reload instructions. Verify focused OIT/clipping, lifecycle,
      publication/binding and compiled-path contracts; reuse passing storage/solver evidence.
  [ ] Completion: independent consumer is usable in game, shader registration/configuration are covered,
      and no screen-space temporal history or procedural view-density path is required. Appearance
      remains user acceptance, not established by these incremental checks.

Phase 8 - Evaluate acceleration and update cost
  Depends on: Phase 7; Phase 1 initial acceleration decision.
  Outcome: a justified acceleration choice accounts for maintenance as well as traversal savings.
  [ ] Measure the selected baseline narrowly: density, occupancy, direct, diffuse, full-field copy and
      view costs, plus actual traversal/work counts and memory. Separate steady and changing content.
  [ ] Evaluate signed versus unsigned distance bounds and hybrid traversal against coarse DDA.
      Prototype only if the recorded feasibility/cost analysis warrants it; otherwise record explicit
      deferral and rationale without claiming a measured distance-field comparison.
  [ ] For any distance prototype, establish conservative distances to all potentially nonzero filtered
      density, accounting for anisotropic cells, quantization and reconstruction error. Do not use a
      visible isosurface threshold or assume hardware-interpolated distances are automatically safe.
  [ ] For any prototype, repair/revoke nonlocal certificates on density additions before publication;
      retain safe smaller bounds on removals. Fall back to safe DDA/no skipping during repair. Include
      recenter/domain changes, guards and all three ray consumers in the safety contract.
  [ ] Compare implemented alternatives including construction/update time, memory and weather backlog;
      preserve occupied integration semantics. Keep only the justified selected strategy and remove
      rejected experimental paths/resources. Do not require both structures in ordinary rendering.
  [ ] Investigate diffuse-copy cost only if measured as a bottleneck; an alternate publication scheme
      requires a separately recorded design decision, not an automatic expansion of this phase.
  [ ] Verify affected conservative traversal/publication contracts with incremental checks; document
      the selected algorithm and distinguish analysis from measured results. No quality thresholds.
  [ ] Completion: selected acceleration has honest total-cost evidence and safe density-update semantics;
      all unimplemented alternatives are explicitly deferred, with no misleading comparison claim.

Phase 9 - Qualify the frozen candidate and reconcile documentation
  Depends on: Phase 8.
  Outcome: measured total cost, memory and user appearance determine candidate acceptance.
  [ ] Freeze the candidate and run canonical packaging/required final checks once. Verify delivered
      assets, selectable settings and cleanup; do not treat older candidate receipts as qualification.
  [ ] Measure total/per-pass GPU time and resident/peak memory at stated hardware/settings/resolution.
      Include startup, steady views, camera motion, wind, evolving weather, light transitions and
      recenter/replacement. Report update spikes, density/lighting backlog, age and fallback coverage.
  [ ] Compare matched view resolutions and label default-resolution differences. Separate illumination
      amortization from per-pixel view cost; disclose running-game contention and measurement limits.
  [ ] Obtain user-run appearance review for shape/thin layers, volume continuity, grid/seam motion,
      stable lighting, leakage, fallback transitions and stale-weather response. Never launch the
      game, invent acceptance, or replace review with automated approximation thresholds.
  [ ] Reconcile all proposal requirements and selected decisions with delivered code, documentation and
      focused evidence. Audit removable ownership and ensure no rejected prototype dependencies remain.
  [ ] Record acceptance or concrete outstanding limitations. If quality/memory/cost is unacceptable,
      retain candidate status and propose the next decision rather than silently shrinking coverage,
      adding procedural density or restoring a screen-space temporal dependency.
  [ ] Completion: package, correctness, GPU measurements and human appearance results are distinguished;
      all required acceptance is satisfied or explicitly left open. Do not remove/promote the older
      candidates without the user's separate replacement decision.

Final acceptance
  [ ] View, direct and diffuse consumers use the persistent 3D density and reusable lighting fields.
  [ ] Agreed memory/feature coverage, bounded updates, conservative traversal and lifecycle hold.
  [ ] User accepts appearance and measured total cost at the stated configuration; no FPS guarantee
      is inferred from architecture or headless tests.
  [ ] Proposal/current docs match implementation; outstanding work and deferred alternatives are explicit.
